    <h4>Founder / Protocol Engineer | <a href="https://after-key-web.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AfterKey</a> — Non-Custodial Crypto Inheritance Protocol (Solana)</h4>
    <p><em>2026 – present</em></p>
    <p>
      A dead-man's-switch inheritance protocol that lets Solana users pass assets to chosen beneficiaries without ever sharing private keys — addressing the billions in crypto permanently lost to owner death.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Authored a 16-instruction Anchor/Rust program implementing a four-state vault machine (Active → InChallenge → Released → Closed) with owner-configurable inactivity timers, a challenge window, and single-signature veto; supports SOL and SPL token custody via PDA-owned vaults and associated token accounts</li>
      <li>Designed for trustless completion: inheritance finalization and pro-rata distribution are permissionless, so claims settle even if the company ceases to exist — distribution targets are read from on-chain state and can never be supplied by the caller</li>
      <li>Built a 63-case test suite on LiteSVM covering the full instruction × state × signer matrix with exact error-code assertions, clock-warped timing-boundary tests, and adversarial cases (account substitution, spoofed claimants, share-arithmetic invariants)</li>
